            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This dip is great and I've made it several times. Even though I make a couple of changes and call it clams casino dip, the rest of the recipe is the same. First, I always double this recipe. I also don't use the cheese. Instead I add one of the cans of clams with it's juice so it's not to dry. Next I add 3 - 6 slices of raw bacon cut very small, (it's best to do this when the bacon's frozen), which cooks completely during the alloted time. I also use a small jar of pimentos, minced, for color. Hope you enjoy."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "vcaprice"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is very similar to an old one a friend of mine gave me years ago. The changes I made were, did not drain the clams and simmered for about 20 min with juice of 1/2 lemon, used 3 dashes of hot sauce and a few pinches of cayenne, used grated Velveeta cheese instead of regular cheddar, then added about a half cup of parmesan/romano cheese on top and coated with paprika. This was the recipe that I had. Turned out great! One of my husbands favorite!",
            "datePublished": "2025-12-31T15:08:56.161Z"
          },
          {
